Who is the most important person in the kingdom?
At that time, the disciples came to Jesus and asked him, saying, "Who is the most important person in the kingdom of heaven?"
Jesus called a little child to him. He stood him in the midst of them.
Jesus, peace be upon him, said, "Truly, I say to you, unless you are converted and become like children, you will not enter the kingdom of heaven."
O human, you must even be faster, free from pride, as this child was, the most important in the kingdom of heaven.
Anyone who welcomes a little child like this in my name welcomes me.
But what if someone causes one of these little ones who believe in me to sin? If he causes them to sin, it would be better for him to have a large millstone hung around his neck and to be drowned at the bottom of the sea.
Oh, what a terrible thing it will be for the world because of the things that lead people into sin! Things like that must come. But oh, what a terrible thing for those who cause it!
If your hand or foot is causing you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of heaven with one hand or one foot, than to go to hell with both hands and both feet. In hell, the fire burns forever.
If your sight is causing you to sin, pluck it out and throw it away. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of heaven with one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into hellfire. The story of the lost sheep.
