The Kingdom of Heaven is like a king who wanted to collect all the money that was owed to him by his servants.
And as the king began to do this, a man to whom he owed millions of dollars was brought to him.
The man was not able to pay. Therefore, his master gave an order. The man, his wife, his children, and everything he possessed had to be sold to pay what he owed.
The servant knelt before his master and pleaded, "Give me some time." He promised, "I will return everything."
His master pitied him, so he pardoned what was due from him and set him free.
But then that servant went out and found one of the other servants who owed him a few dollars. He seized him and began to strangle him. 'Pay what you owe me!' he said.
The other server got down on his knees. "Give me some time," he begged him. "I'll pay you back."
But the first servant refused. Instead, he went and ordered the man to be thrown into prison. The man was to stay there until he could repay what he owed.
The other servants saw what happened. This disturbed them greatly. They went and told their master everything that happened.
Then the master called the first servant. Then he said to him, "Where is our evil servant?" "I have forgiven you all your debt."
