They said, "Give us good news, O Jesus! Who is the one who struck you?" He said, "Behold, the one who delivered me over to you is with you here; it is he who has given you over to me." Pilate said, "I am not a Jew, am I? Your own nation and the chief priests have handed you over to me; what have you done?" Jesus answered, "My kingdom is not of this world; if my kingdom were of this world, my followers would be fighting to prevent my arrest by the Jews. My kingdom is not of this world." Pilate said, "So you are a king?" Jesus answered, "You say that I am a king. For this I was born, and for this I have come into the world—to testify to the truth. Everyone who belongs to the truth listens to my voice." Pilate said to him, "What is truth?" After he had said this, he went out to the Jews and told them, "I find no basis for a charge against him. But it is custom for the one condemned to death to be released; whom do you want me to release for you?" They cried out in unison, "Not this man, but Barabbas!" Now Barabbas was a revolutionary. Pilate addressed the crowd again, "What shall I do, then, with the man you call the King of the Jews?" "Crucify him!" the chief priests and the elders demanded. "We have no king but Caesar!" Pilate said, "Here I am, then, bringing him out to you for judgment. I myself find no basis for a charge against him." When Jesus came out wearing the crown of thorns and the purple robe, Pilate said to the chief priests and officers of the Jews, "Behold your king!" They cried out, "Crucify him, crucify him!" Pilate said to them, "Take him yourselves and crucify him, for I find no basis for a charge against him." The chief priests answered, "We ourselves have seen what he said to the people and what he did by healing those who were lame and blind, and by causing the dead to rise. For this reason the people are following him, for they have been impressed by the miraculous signs that he is performing." Pilate said to them, "So you yourselves are saying 