Once Jesus was walking alongside the Sea of Galilee. There he saw Simon and his brother Andrew. They were throwing a net into the lake, for they were fishermen.
"Hello. Follow me," said Jesus. "I will make you fishers of men."
Immediately they left their nets and followed him.
Then Jesus walked a little further. And he saw Simon, also called Peter, Andrew's brother, and also James and John, sons of Zebedee, and others. They were in a boat mending their fishing nets.
Immediately he called them. So they left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired hands. Then they followed Jesus. And Jesus expelled the devil.
Jesus and those who were with him went to Capernaum. And when the Sabbath came, he went to the synagogue. And he began to teach there.
People admired his teaching. He taught them as if he were an authority. He did not speak like a professor of law.
And suddenly, the cry of a man rose up in their midst. He was possessed by an evil spirit. He said:
"What do you want from us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are. You are the Holy One of God indeed!"
"Be quiet!" Jesus said firmly. "Come out of him!"
So the devil cast him out violently, then he came out of him with a great cry.
All the people were amazed. And some of them asked each other, "What is this? A new teaching! And with authority! Even the demons are submitting to him, crying out, 'What have you to do with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are, the Holy One of God!'"
News of Jesus spread quickly throughout Galilee. Jesus healed many people.
Jesus and those with him left the temple and immediately went, along with James and John, to the house of Simon and Judas.
Simon's mother-in-law was lying in bed. She was suffering from a fever. They told Jesus about her.
He went to her, took her hand and helped her up. The fever left her. Then she began to serve them.
That evening, after sunset, the people brought to Jesus all who were sick. They also brought all who were possessed by demons.
A large crowd of townspeople gathered at the entrance.
Jesus healed many of them. They suffered from all kinds of diseases. He also drove out many demons. But he did not allow the demons to speak, because they knew who he was. Jesus prays in a quiet place.
The morning came very early and it was still dark. Jesus got up and left the house. He went to a place where he could be alone. There he prayed.
Simon and his friends went to look for Jesus.
When they found him, they shouted at the top of their voices, "Everyone is looking for you!"
Jesus replied, saying, "Let us go to another place. I want to go to the neighboring towns. I must preach in them also. For this reason I came."
He traveled throughout Galilee. He preached in their synagogues. He cast out demons from those who were possessed. Jesus heals a man who suffered from a skin disease.
A man who had a skin disease came to Jesus. He fell to his knees before the Lord Jesus and said, "If you are willing to make me clean, then it is within your power to do so."
Jesus was filled with deep concern. He reached out and touched the man. "I am willing to do this," he said. "Be 'clean'!"
Immediately the illness left him. He was cured.
Jesus immediately dispatched him, and he gave the man a strong warning.
"Don't tell anyone about this," he said. "Go and show yourself to the priest. Make the sacrifices that Moses commanded. You will be a witness to the priest and the people that you are 'clean.'"
But the man went out and began to talk openly. He spread the news to everyone. So Jesus could no longer openly enter a town. Instead, he stayed outside in remote places. Yet people kept coming to him from everywhere.
Jesus healed a man who could not walk.
After several days, Jesus returned to Capernaum. The people heard that he had returned home.
